Thread affinity on OHOS: declare what musl hides, call what musl has.

ggml picks its affinity implementation by platform, and OHOS falls into the
__linux__ branch. Two things there do not hold on this sysroot:

  cpu_set_t, CPU_ZERO, CPU_SET   musl has them, behind _GNU_SOURCE. The OHOS
                                 toolchain passes -D_XOPEN_SOURCE=600, which
                                 hides them. Defining _GNU_SOURCE is enough.
  pthread_setaffinity_np         musl does not have it at all, under any guard.
                                 But it does have sched_setaffinity, and ggml
                                 already calls that on the one other platform
                                 with the same gap: Android. Widening that
                                 branch to OHOS reuses the fix upstream wrote.

sched_setaffinity(0, ...) pins the calling thread, which is what this function
is called on, so the two calls agree here.

An earlier version of this patch narrowed __linux__ to __gnu_linux__ instead,
sending OHOS to the "unsupported platform" stub. That built, and it was wrong
twice over: it silently dropped affinity, and it called -D_GNU_SOURCE a
symptom-level fix when _GNU_SOURCE is in fact half of the real one. llama.cpp's
checkout carries this same patch, in this same shape, for the same sysroot --
see llama-ggml-ohos-affinity.patch, which is this diff against a newer ggml.

What affinity is worth on this device has not been measured. The thread-count
sweep is the closest thing, and it found 4/6/8 within 2%. So this patch is
"do not silently drop upstream's behavior", not "known to be faster".

--- a/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
+++ b/src/ggml-cpu/ggml-cpu.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 #define _CRT_SECURE_NO_DEPRECATE // Disables "unsafe" warnings on Windows
 #define _USE_MATH_DEFINES // For M_PI on MSVC
+#define _GNU_SOURCE 1 // OHOS: cpu_set_t/CPU_ZERO live behind this guard in musl sched.h
 
 #include "ggml-backend-impl.h"
 #include "ggml-backend.h"
@@ -2650,7 +2651,7 @@ static bool ggml_thread_apply_affinity(const bool * mask) {
         }
     }
 
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
+#if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__OHOS__) // OHOS has sched_setaffinity but no pthread_setaffinity_np
     err = sched_setaffinity(0, sizeof(cpuset), &cpuset);
     if (err < 0) {
         err = errno;
